# P3a (docs/tp4-p2p-host.md section 8): the peer-to-peer KV restore on the cards, standalone (scripts/ci/tp4_p2p_restore_probe.py).
# The cache drive's identity (the kernel's model and serial for the node against the status file's by_id) and R1's two readings (controller state, namespace size) are checked and printed before the first byte is written; anything
# but `live` refuses. Then one card first (the widest link), every published card, the known object read from the drive into the cards' staging buffers, checked against the host's checksums,
# copied into scratch KV caches and compared byte for byte; a negative arm (one flipped byte on the drive: refused, nothing written, passes when put back); the windows and the p2pmem pools released.
# READ: the last 'P3A verdict=PASS' line (read_gbps, restore_gbps, check_ms_per_chunk, write_ms_per_chunk). NOT-MEASURED (exit 2) is a refusal or a setup failure with nothing written; FAIL is a result.
# WHICH drive and WHICH cards: the runner keys C2_NVME_DEVICE and C2_P2PMEM (scripts/ci/c2_cache_drive.py; docs/tp4-kv-nvme.md section 12 (1)), written here as the words `status` (the by_id of the
# host boot unit's status file) and `auto` (every card that publishes p2pmem), so no by-id name, serial or PCI address is in this pushed file or in the log. The step resolves the drive from
# its link now, prints R1 and refuses unless live; the probe then shows from the kernel that the node it was handed is the drive the status file names (no byte is written before).
# NEEDS: the patched tt-kmd loaded for the cards that publish p2pmem (p2pmem/available == size), the cache drive live (R1), Opal-unlocked and not a mounted filesystem, the cards idle (no serving container: the step refuses one), and
# an image that carries the device-op extension (ttnn.qwen_p2p_staging_alloc / _info, qwen_staging_checksum with count=, qwen_write_blocks_from_staging with row_stride=) beside the raw block ops. An image whose extension
# lacks the two keywords still runs (the host falls back to its slow compat mode; the log and report say device_ops=compat), but the restore rate it measures is then the compat one. The probe itself
# runs from the checkout the step mounts at /c2, so it needs the image, not a build of this commit. A reset is the next job's first action (the window is a card window).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env, to be copied over it on a throwaway commit of the window branch; C2_IMAGE_TAG is the image the orchestrator built with the device-op graft.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=p2p-restore
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-p2p-1
C2_NVME_DEVICE=status
C2_P2PMEM=auto
